  "body": "From the re-review of PR #210 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/210#issuecomment-6714959319). A plain two-ring turned bar at n=16 and n=64 is refused in some orientations. main refuses the same cases, as 'mesh is open', so this isn't a regression. The new message wrongly says a non-turned feature crosses the seam. Likely cause (unconfirmed): the fitted axis is slightly off true and `refuse_feature_on_seam`'s 1e-9 rad azimuth tolerance is too tight. CAD-style stepped shafts meshed with a different column count per diameter hit the same confusing message. Also: `rotary_offset.rs` is 401 lines.\n\nDone means: a plain turned bar wraps in every orientation (0 cut tips inside the part), or is refused with a reason that names the real cause; the azimuth tolerance is scaled to the axis-fit's accuracy; and a stepped shaft with mixed column counts either wraps or is refused accurately.",
